{"name":"After Eight","hex":"#3d2e24","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"after","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Behind; later in time; following."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Subsequently to; following in time; later than.","Subsequently to and as a result of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after"},{"term":"eight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 8."]},{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["A numerical value equal to 8; the number occurring after seven and before nine.","Describing a group or set with eight elements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eight"}],"entries":[{"title":"After Eight","blocks":[{"text":"After Eight Mint Chocolate Thins, often referred to as simply After Eights, are a brand of confectionery consisting of a thin peppermint fondant coated in dark chocolate. They were created by Brian Sollitt at Rowntree Company Limited in the UK in 1962 and have been manufactured by Nestlé since its acquisition of Rowntree in 1988."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/After_Eight_chocolate_thin_%28adjusted%29.jpg/330px-After_Eight_chocolate_thin_%28adjusted%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Eight","wikidata":"Q388973"},{"title":"After Eight (album)","blocks":[{"text":"After Eight is the debut studio album by Indonesian-born Dutch singer and songwriter Taco Ockerse, known mononymously as Taco. It was released in November 1982 through RCA Records. The album contains five original songs co-written by Taco, as well as six cover versions of classic pop songs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/After_Eight_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/After_Eight_(album)","wik